00:07:52.772 --> 00:07:53.539
But the only

00:07:53.739 --> 00:07:55.641
polls that she didn't have,

00:07:55.641 --> 00:07:56.943
she didn't make the case at all

00:07:56.943 --> 00:07:57.777
and that she

00:07:57.810 --> 00:07:58.678
she didn't mention

00:07:58.678 --> 00:08:00.179
that she was leading in the polls

00:08:00.179 --> 00:08:01.280
she obviously didn't think

00:08:01.280 --> 00:08:02.415
that was

00:08:02.482 --> 00:08:03.483
a compelling argument

00:08:03.483 --> 00:08:05.251
for the reason that Scott

00:08:05.251 --> 00:08:06.919
said the electability argument

00:08:06.919 --> 00:08:08.855
has sort of faded because of that.

00:08:08.855 --> 00:08:10.356
But on the question of DeSantis,

00:08:10.356 --> 00:08:12.458
and I'd like to ask you guys this,

00:08:13.259 --> 00:08:15.728
it seems to me there were moments

00:08:15.728 --> 00:08:17.463
there, like when he went counter

00:08:17.463 --> 00:08:19.999
to a number of people on Ukraine.

00:08:19.999 --> 00:08:21.267
I was on the other side.

00:08:21.267 --> 00:08:22.101
I'm on the other side

00:08:22.101 --> 00:08:23.302
of this issue personally,

00:08:23.302 --> 00:08:25.204
but I suspect there are a lot of voters

00:08:25.204 --> 00:08:26.405
in these Republican primaries.

00:08:26.405 --> 00:08:28.040
If you follow polls

00:08:28.040 --> 00:08:30.176
who don't want to give more money

00:08:30.443 --> 00:08:31.277
to Ukraine,

00:08:31.277 --> 00:08:33.913
he took a very strong position on that.

00:08:34.113 --> 00:08:36.182
Those kinds of things are memorable

00:08:36.449 --> 00:08:38.217
to people, particularly in the states

00:08:38.217 --> 00:08:40.286
that you've been hanging out in, in Iowa.

00:08:40.286 --> 00:08:41.053
And New Hampshire.

00:08:41.053 --> 00:08:43.089
I suspect a few of those things

00:08:43.322 --> 00:08:45.291
may register with those voter.

00:08:45.291 --> 00:08:46.626
Listen, he unequivocally,

00:08:46.626 --> 00:08:48.060
Governor DeSantis unequivocally

00:08:48.060 --> 00:08:48.961
did better this debate

00:08:48.961 --> 00:08:50.263
than the prior debate.

00:08:50.263 --> 00:08:51.330
I was actually noticing

00:08:51.330 --> 00:08:52.798
you could kind of hear that consultants

00:08:52.798 --> 00:08:53.533
got in the heads

00:08:53.533 --> 00:08:54.767
of some of these candidates.

00:08:54.767 --> 00:08:56.135
He mentioned a story about his wife.

00:08:56.135 --> 00:08:57.303
He tried to show some heart

00:08:57.303 --> 00:08:59.505
about visiting Reagan's gravesite.

00:08:59.672 --> 00:09:01.040
He did give the answer in Ukraine,

00:09:01.040 --> 00:09:02.542
which is a differentiating point.

00:09:02.542 --> 00:09:03.876
The background is for me trying to play

00:09:03.876 --> 00:09:04.877
nice guy this time,

00:09:04.877 --> 00:09:05.978
because the biggest critique

00:09:05.978 --> 00:09:06.779
last time was

00:09:06.779 --> 00:09:07.246
he came off

00:09:07.246 --> 00:09:08.514
so off putting it and like

00:09:08.514 --> 00:09:09.048
it was interesting

00:09:09.048 --> 00:09:10.550
in one of his first answers

00:09:10.550 --> 00:09:11.083
when he was talking

00:09:11.083 --> 00:09:13.185
about unions and striking.

00:09:13.185 --> 00:09:17.156
He expressed sympathy for four workers.

00:09:17.256 --> 00:09:18.124
And I actually thought

00:09:18.124 --> 00:09:19.358
that was one of his strongest moments

00:09:19.358 --> 00:09:20.726
If there is one question

00:09:20.726 --> 00:09:21.661
that put on display

00:09:21.661 --> 00:09:23.462
how different today's Republican Party

00:09:23.462 --> 00:09:25.331
is than the one of ten years ago.

00:09:25.331 --> 00:09:27.166
It was the answer around the strikes

00:09:27.166 --> 00:09:29.302
going on this, you know, Okay.

00:09:29.468 --> 00:09:30.469
Well, now hearing that

00:09:30.469 --> 00:09:31.170
some of these people

00:09:31.170 --> 00:09:33.072
are taking a much more pro-worker stance,

00:09:33.072 --> 00:09:34.373
it has less to do with,

00:09:34.373 --> 00:09:34.674
you know,

00:09:34.674 --> 00:09:35.775
what you're giving to shareholders

00:09:35.775 --> 00:09:36.442
or the free market.

00:09:36.442 --> 00:09:37.710
It's much more about workers.

00:09:37.710 --> 00:09:38.210
It's much more

00:09:38.210 --> 00:09:40.246
Pat Buchanan's party than it is,

00:09:40.246 --> 00:09:40.580
you know,

00:09:40.580 --> 00:09:41.847
Paul Ryan and Mitt Romney's party.

